From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mimo-v2: MTP draft widths with a measured per-request policy

VLLM_MIMO26_DRAFT_WIDTHS=1 (default 0 = unchanged; MiMo-V2 MTP, k > 1):
when the scheduler schedules a batch it decides the draft width k for it
(SchedulerOutput.mimo26_next_draft_k). Every scheduled request records
mimo26_drafted = k, async placeholders are exactly k, and its next
verification consumes exactly those k drafts (a manual vllm_xargs.spec_k caps
it; preemption resets it). spec_k is parsed, validated and limited only in
the MiMo module vllm/v1/core/sched/mimo26_spec_k.py, reached through two
MiMo-architecture-gated call sites next to DeepSeek's (InputProcessor after
params.verify() -> HTTP 400; Scheduler.add_request -> verification limit);
the generic protocol / sampling_params code is untouched and every other
model ignores the key.
One width per scheduled batch keeps the verification uniform: exact decode
CUDA graphs are captured for every width 1 + k on every PP stage and for the
multi-module MTP drafter (whose input is the last step's 1 + k). The drafter
samples only the first k drafts (draft lm_head + sampling skipped beyond k;
one FULL drafter graph per draft count), but every head still runs its
forward so its own KV cache stays current; a skipped head's placeholder
input is a never-verified token whose slot is re-prefilled next step like a
rejected draft's. Narrower verification removes verify rows (each widens the
routed-expert union of every MoE layer) and the skipped draft heads.

VLLM_MIMO26_ADAPTIVE_WIDTH=1 (default 0; needs the above): the DeepSeek
V4.1 measured verification policy (deepseek-v4.1-flash adaptive/0009) as
generalised to MTP k <= K for Qwen3.8 (qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4 0009), with
MiMo's measured step costs: per-position at-risk acceptance with 0.95 decay,
measured output/time blended with one calibrated predicted block, 98 %-of-peak
cold choice with +3 %, then +3 % plus ratio/paired-prefix uncertainty gates,
at most one width of growth per decision, manual spec_k first, failure keeps
K. Batch width: between the smallest and largest member choice, the width
with the highest summed relative policy score. Each decision starts from
the width the request actually ran at (the batch width), so a member that was
outvoted keeps learning instead of freezing at its own earlier choice, and
growth (cold rule included) is at most one width above it. Once trimmed, a
request re-decides every 8 fresh feedbacks (a decision per request per step
cost ~2 ms of engine-core CPU per 8-request PP batch at c32). A position the
request has not been verified at is priced at 0.9 x the previous position's
estimate (DeepSeek: 0.5 x), so a request below K can still earn growth; new
requests start at the most common last width of the recently finished ones
(K until 4 have finished), so arrivals do not widen whole batches to K. The
per-request stamps stay in the policy, not on the pickled SchedulerOutput.

diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/sched/async_scheduler.py b/vllm/v1/core/sched/async_scheduler.py
index b5e863b..e8f3678 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/core/sched/async_scheduler.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/sched/async_scheduler.py
@@ -74,6 +74,11 @@ class AsyncScheduler(Scheduler):
             # Add placeholders for the new draft/spec tokens.
             # We will update the actual spec token ids in the worker process.
             limit = getattr(request, "verification_draft_limit", None)
+            drafted = getattr(request, "mimo26_drafted", None)
+            if drafted is not None:
+                # MiMo draft widths: placeholders for exactly the drafts this
+                # step generates (a manual spec_k caps the verification).
+                limit = drafted if limit is None else min(drafted, limit)
             request.spec_token_ids = (
                 self._spec_token_placeholders if limit is None
                 else self._spec_token_placeholders[:limit]
diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/sched/mimo26_spec_k.py b/vllm/v1/core/sched/mimo26_spec_k.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..eb43607
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/sched/mimo26_spec_k.py
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+"""MiMo-V2.6 request-local MTP draft width (``vllm_xargs.spec_k``).
+
+``vllm_xargs`` already reaches ``SamplingParams.extra_args`` unchanged for every
+model. Only MiMo-V2 architectures consult this module (two architecture-gated
+call sites: input validation and scheduler admission, next to DeepSeek's);
+every other model ignores the key exactly like the unpatched engine. Valid
+only with VLLM_MIMO26_DRAFT_WIDTHS=1 and MTP (0007).
+"""
+import os
+
+from vllm.exceptions import VLLMValidationError
+
+
+def is_mimo26(model_config) -> bool:
+    return any(a.startswith("MiMoV2") for a in (model_config.architectures or []))
+
+
+def _widths_enabled(spec) -> bool:
+    return (os.environ.get("VLLM_MIMO26_DRAFT_WIDTHS", "0") == "1"
+            and spec is not None and spec.method == "mtp")
+
+
+def validate_request(extra_args, speculative_config) -> None:
+    """Front-end validation; failures surface as HTTP 400."""
+    if not extra_args or "spec_k" not in extra_args:
+        return
+    value = extra_args["spec_k"]
+    if type(value) is not int or value < 0:
+        raise VLLMValidationError(
+            "vllm_xargs.spec_k must be a nonnegative integer",
+            parameter="vllm_xargs.spec_k",
+        )
+    if not _widths_enabled(speculative_config):
+        raise VLLMValidationError(
+            "spec_k requires VLLM_MIMO26_DRAFT_WIDTHS=1 and MTP",
+            parameter="vllm_xargs.spec_k",
+        )
+    if not 0 <= value <= speculative_config.num_speculative_tokens:
+        raise VLLMValidationError(
+            "spec_k must be an integer between 0 and configured draft count",
+            parameter="vllm_xargs.spec_k",
+        )
+
+
+def draft_limit(request, spec, num_spec_tokens: int,
+                use_v2_model_runner: bool) -> int | None:
+    """Scheduler admission: the request's verified-draft limit, or None."""
+    params = request.sampling_params
+    extra = params.extra_args if params is not None else None
+    limit = extra.get("spec_k") if extra else None
+    if limit is None:
+        return None
+    if not use_v2_model_runner or not _widths_enabled(spec):
+        raise ValueError("spec_k requires MiMo MTP draft widths")
+    if type(limit) is not int or not 0 <= limit <= num_spec_tokens:
+        raise ValueError("spec_k must be an integer in the configured draft range")
+    return limit
diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/sched/mimo26_verification_policy.py b/vllm/v1/core/sched/mimo26_verification_policy.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..39b9898
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vllm/v1/core/sched/mimo26_verification_policy.py
@@ -0,0 +1,452 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+"""Request-local measured MTP draft width for MiMo-V2.6 (CPU only).
+
+VLLM_MIMO26_ADAPTIVE_WIDTH=1 (default 0 = unchanged; requires
+VLLM_MIMO26_DRAFT_WIDTHS=1). The DeepSeek V4.1 measured verification policy
+(models/deepseek-v4.1-flash adaptive/0009) as generalised from DSpark k<=5 to
+MTP k<=K for Qwen3.8 (qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4 0009), with MiMo's cost table:
+
+* per request, per verified width: discounted (decay 0.95) at-risk acceptance
+  per draft position, output tokens and CPU-visible feedback recurrence time;
+* each width's measured output/time is blended with one predicted pseudo-block
+  (prefix-acceptance expectation x MiMo's measured step cost at the current
+  concurrency), calibrated to the current width's observed level;
+* a cold first trim needs +3 % over the incumbent (choosing the widest width
+  within 98 % of the peak); afterwards a change needs +3 % plus a ratio and
+  paired-prefix uncertainty gate; growth is at most one width per decision;
+* manual vllm_xargs.spec_k always wins; any policy failure keeps full K.
+
+The choice is a draft count: when the scheduler schedules a batch it decides
+how many drafts the MTP drafter generates for it, and the next step verifies
+exactly those drafts (growing the width means drafting more next time). The
+decode graphs are exact only for uniform batches, so the choices of the
+requests in one scheduled batch are combined into one count: the width
+(between the smallest and largest member choice) with the highest summed
+relative policy score.
+No task labels, external IO, CUDA objects or fixed observation windows.
+"""
+
+import math
+import os
+import time
+from types import SimpleNamespace
+
+
+def mimo26_widths_enabled(vllm_config) -> bool:
+    """VLLM_MIMO26_DRAFT_WIDTHS=1, MTP with more than one draft, MiMo-V2."""
+    spec = vllm_config.speculative_config
+    return bool(
+        os.environ.get("VLLM_MIMO26_DRAFT_WIDTHS", "0") == "1"
+        and spec is not None
+        and spec.method == "mtp"
+        and spec.num_speculative_tokens > 1
+        and any(
+            a.startswith("MiMoV2") for a in vllm_config.model_config.architectures
+        )
+    )
+
+# Measured per-request step time (ms) on 4x CMP 170HX, PP4 13/13/13/9, MTP
+# parallel heads, by concurrency and drafts generated = verified k = 1..3
+# (index k-1), mean over counting/code/prose (fixed-width runs k=1..3, 500 tokens),
+# made non-decreasing in k. Only the ratios between widths matter: the policy
+# calibrates the level to the current width's observed recurrence.
+COST_MS = {
+    1: (17.2, 20.3, 23.3),
+    8: (38.8, 38.9, 46.5),
+    32: (47.2, 65.5, 74.0),
+}
+
+
+def costs(c, k_max):
+    cs = sorted(COST_MS)
+
+    def row(v):
+        v = list(v)[:k_max]
+        while len(v) < k_max:  # extrapolate linearly in k if K > table width
+            v.append(v[-1] + (v[-1] - v[-2] if len(v) > 1 else 0.0))
+        return [x / 1000 for x in v]
+
+    if c <= cs[0]:
+        return row(COST_MS[cs[0]])
+    for lo, hi in zip(cs, cs[1:]):
+        if c <= hi:
+            w = (c - lo) / (hi - lo)
+            return row(a * (1 - w) + b * w for a, b in zip(COST_MS[lo], COST_MS[hi]))
+    return row(COST_MS[cs[-1]])
+
+
+class Policy:
+    def __init__(self, k_max, decay=0.95, prediction_weight=1.0):
+        if not 0 <= decay < 1 or not 0 < prediction_weight <= 100 or k_max < 1:
+            raise ValueError("invalid config")
+        K = self.K = int(k_max)
+        self.decay = float(decay)
+        self.w = float(prediction_weight)
+        self.k = K
+        self.n = [0.0] * K
+        self.y = [0.0] * K
+        self.t = [0.0] * K
+        self.risk = [0.0] * K
+        self.success = [0.0] * K
+        self.prior = 1.0
+        self.epoch = None
+        self.diagnostics = {}
+        self.latest = None
+        self.trimmed = False
+        self.history = [[0.0] * (K + 1) for _ in range(K)]
+        self.q = [0.0] * K
+        self.y2 = [0.0] * K
+        self.t2 = [0.0] * K
+        self.yt = [0.0] * K
+
+    def observe(self, e):
+        K = self.K
+        k = e["k"]
+        a = e["accepted"]
+        dt = e["seconds"]
+        if not 1 <= k <= K or not 0 <= a <= k:
+            raise ValueError("invalid feedback")
+        self.latest = (k, bool(e["timing_valid"]))
+        d = self.decay
+        for row in self.history:
+            for i in range(len(row)):
+                row[i] *= d
+        self.history[k - 1][a] += 1
+        self.prior *= self.decay
+        if self.epoch != e["load_epoch"]:
+            self.n = [0.0] * K
+            self.y = [0.0] * K
+            self.t = [0.0] * K
+            self.epoch = e["load_epoch"]
+            self.q = [0.0] * K
+            self.y2 = [0.0] * K
+            self.t2 = [0.0] * K
+            self.yt = [0.0] * K
+        for j in range(K):
+            self.n[j] *= self.decay
+            self.y[j] *= self.decay
+            self.t[j] *= self.decay
+            self.q[j] *= self.decay**2
+            self.y2[j] *= self.decay
+            self.t2[j] *= self.decay
+            self.yt[j] *= self.decay
+            self.risk[j] *= self.decay
+            self.success[j] *= self.decay
+            if j < k:
+                self.risk[j] += 1
+                self.success[j] += a > j
+        if e["timing_valid"]:
+            j = k - 1
+            y = e["output_tokens"]
+            self.n[j] += 1
+            self.y[j] += y
+            self.t[j] += dt
+            self.q[j] += 1
+            self.y2[j] += y * y
+            self.t2[j] += dt * dt
+            self.yt[j] += y * dt
+
+    def choose(self, context):
+        K = self.K
+        self.k = context["current_k"]
+        p = []
+        previous = 1.0
+        for n, s in zip(self.risk, self.success):
+            # Pseudo-observation weight 1 at 0.9 x the previous position's
+            # estimate (DeepSeek: 0.5 x). A position the request has not been
+            # verified at is then priced near the last measured one, so a
+            # request running below K can still earn growth (counting/code
+            # at c32), while a low first-position acceptance (prose) cannot.
+            previous = min(
+                previous, (s + self.prior + 0.9 * previous) / (n + self.prior + 1)
+            )
+            p.append(previous)
+        E = [1 + sum(p[:k]) for k in range(1, K + 1)]
+        C = costs(context["concurrency"], K)
+        # Calibrate predictions to the current observed level; keep ratios.
+        i = self.k - 1
+        scale = self.y[i] / self.n[i] / E[i] if self.n[i] else 1.0
+        time_scale = self.t[i] / self.n[i] / C[i] if self.n[i] else 1.0
+        predicted_y = [e * scale for e in E]
+        predicted_t = [c * time_scale for c in C]
+        scores = [
+            (y + self.w * e) / (t + self.w * c)
+            for y, t, e, c in zip(self.y, self.t, predicted_y, predicted_t)
+        ]
+        se = []
+        for j in range(K):
+            n = self.n[j]
+            if n <= 0:
+                se.append(0.0)
+                continue
+            rate = self.y[j] / self.t[j]
+            variance = max(
+                0.0, (self.y2[j] - 2 * rate * self.yt[j] + rate * rate * self.t2[j]) / n
+            )
+            ess = min(n, n * n / self.q[j])
+            se.append((variance + 1.0) ** 0.5 / (self.t[j] / n) / (ess + 1) ** 0.5)
+        fractions = [t / (t + self.w * c) for t, c in zip(self.t, predicted_t)]
+        gate = [f * (s * s + se[self.k - 1] ** 2) ** 0.5 for f, s in zip(fractions, se)]
+        hist = self.history[i]
+        mass = sum(hist)
+        model_se = []
+        for j in range(K):
+            if j >= i:
+                model_se.append(0.0)
+                continue
+            diffs = [
+                ((1 + min(a, j + 1)) / C[j] - (1 + min(a, self.k)) / C[i])
+                * scale
+                / time_scale
+                for a in range(K + 1)
+            ]
+            mean = sum(w * d for w, d in zip(hist, diffs)) / mass if mass else 0.0
+            variance = (
+                sum(w * (d - mean) ** 2 for w, d in zip(hist, diffs)) / mass
+                if mass
+                else 0.0
+            )
+            model_se.append((variance / (mass + 1)) ** 0.5)
+        gate = [(a * a + b * b) ** 0.5 for a, b in zip(gate, model_se)]
+        ready = bool(
+            self.latest and self.latest[0] == self.k and self.latest[1]
+        )
+        best = self.k
+        if ready:
+            if not self.trimmed:
+                peak = max(scores)
+                cold = max(k for k in range(1, K + 1) if scores[k - 1] >= 0.98 * peak)
+                # The current width is the batch width actually run, which
+                # may be below this request's own earlier choice: grow at
+                # most one width per decision here too.
+                cold = min(cold, self.k + 1)
+                if scores[cold - 1] > scores[best - 1] * 1.03:
+                    best = cold
+            else:
+                for k in range(1, min(K, self.k + 1) + 1):
+                    if (
+                        scores[k - 1] - scores[self.k - 1]
+                        > 0.03 * scores[self.k - 1] + gate[k - 1]
+                        and scores[k - 1] > scores[best - 1]
+                    ):
+                        best = k
+        if best < K:
+            self.trimmed = True
+        self.diagnostics = dict(score=scores, se=se, gate=gate, ready=ready)
+        return best
+
+
+class MeasuredWidthPolicy:
+    """Scheduler adapter: generation-pinned per-request entries.
+
+    Only valid actual-width feedback advances selection; the retained width is
+    used between decisions. Feedback recurrence is CPU-visible cadence (PP
+    cadence and queueing included), not GPU kernel time.
+    """
+
+    def __init__(self, logger, k_max, decay=0.95, decide_every=8):
+        if isinstance(decay, bool) or not math.isfinite(decay) or not 0 <= decay < 1:
+            raise ValueError("invalid history decay")
+        self.logger = logger
+        self.K = int(k_max)
+        self.decay = decay
+        # Once trimmed, re-decide a request's width only every decide_every
+        # fresh feedbacks (before that, on every feedback): the evidence horizon is ~20 blocks
+        # (decay 0.95) and growth is one width per decision anyway, while a
+        # decision per request per step is CPU on the engine-core thread
+        # (measured ~2 ms per 8-request PP batch at c32 on this host).
+        self.decide_every = max(1, int(decide_every))
+
+        self.active = {}
+        self.generation = 0
+        self.feedback_time = None
+        self.warned = False
+        self.stamps = {}
+        # Admission: a new request starts at the most common last width of
+        # the recently finished requests (K when none), so arrivals do not
+        # widen their whole batch to K for their first steps.
+        self.recent = []
+        logger.info(
+            "MiMo measured MTP draft width policy: K=%d decay=%s",
+            self.K,
+            decay,
+        )
+
+    def admit(self, request):
+        if getattr(request, "verification_draft_limit", None) is None:
+            self.generation += 1
+            start = self._prior()
+            plugin = Policy(self.K, self.decay)
+            plugin.k = start
+            # Below K the start is a trim already: gated rule, +1 growth.
+            plugin.trimmed = start < self.K
+            self.active[request.request_id] = SimpleNamespace(
+                plugin=plugin,
+                k=start,
+                generation=self.generation,
+                previous=None,
+                fresh=False,
+                failed=False,
+                pending=0,
+                decided=False,
+            )
+
+    def _prior(self):
+        if len(self.recent) < 4:
+            return self.K
+        counts = [0] * (self.K + 1)
+        for k in self.recent:
+            counts[k] += 1
+        return max(range(1, self.K + 1), key=lambda k: (counts[k], k))
+
+    def forget(self, request_id):
+        entry = self.active.pop(request_id, None)
+        if entry is not None and entry.decided and not entry.failed:
+            self.recent.append(entry.k)
+            del self.recent[:-32]
+
+    def _fail(self, entry, exc):
+        # Fail closed to full K. No retry until the next admission.
+        entry.failed = True
+        entry.k = self.K
+        entry.fresh = False
+        if not self.warned:
+            self.logger.warning(
+                "MiMo width policy failure (%s); full K retained",
+                type(exc).__name__,
+            )
+            self.warned = True
+
+    def manages(self, request):
+        return request.request_id in self.active
+
+    def next_width(self, requests, concurrency):
+        """Next draft count for one scheduled batch.
+
+        Each managed request's measured choice is updated only after fresh
+        feedback. One batch count is needed (exact uniform graphs): among the
+        widths between the smallest and the largest member choice, take the
+        one with the highest summed relative score, i.e. each request's
+        policy score at that width divided by its score at its own choice. A
+        single request (or a batch that agrees) gets exactly its choice."""
+        entries = []
+        for r in requests:
+            entry = self.active.get(r.request_id)
+            if entry is None:
+                continue
+            if (
+                not entry.failed
+                and entry.fresh
+                # Every feedback until the first decision and while untrimmed,
+                # then every decide_every feedbacks.
+                and (
+                    not entry.decided
+                    or not entry.plugin.trimmed
+                    or entry.pending >= self.decide_every
+                )
+            ):
+                try:
+                    # Decide from the width the request actually ran at (the
+                    # batch width), not its previous own choice: a member
+                    # outvoted in the batch combination otherwise never sees
+                    # feedback at its own width and its choice freezes.
+                    latest = entry.plugin.latest
+                    current = latest[0] if latest else entry.k
+                    k = entry.plugin.choose(
+                        dict(current_k=current, concurrency=concurrency)
+                    )
+                    if type(k) is not int or not 1 <= k <= self.K or k > current + 1:
+                        raise ValueError("policy width outside allowed transition")
+                    entry.k = k
+                    entry.fresh = False
+                    entry.decided = True
+                    entry.pending = 0
+                    entry.scores = list(entry.plugin.diagnostics.get("score", ()))
+                except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 - fail closed
+                    self._fail(entry, exc)
+            entries.append(entry)
+        if not entries:
+            return 1
+        lo = min(e.k for e in entries)
+        hi = max(e.k for e in entries)
+        if lo == hi:
+            return hi
+
+        def utility(k):
+            total = 0.0
+            for e in entries:
+                scores = getattr(e, "scores", None)
+                if e.failed or not scores or len(scores) < self.K or scores[e.k - 1] <= 0:
+                    # No usable model: this member only accepts its own width
+                    # or wider (never narrower than an unknown preference).
+                    total += 1.0 if k >= e.k else 0.0
+                else:
+                    total += scores[k - 1] / scores[e.k - 1]
+            return total
+
+        # Ties prefer the wider width (as the per-request cold rule does).
+        return max(range(lo, hi + 1), key=lambda k: (utility(k), k))
+
+    def scheduled(self, output, residents, concurrency):
+        if not self.active:
+            return
+        now = time.perf_counter()
+        key = tuple(sorted(r.request_id for r in residents))
+        prefilling = any(r.is_prefill_chunk for r in residents)
+        stamps = {}
+        for rid, drafts in output.scheduled_spec_decode_tokens.items():
+            entry = self.active.get(rid)
+            if entry is not None and not entry.failed:
+                stamps[rid] = (entry.generation, now, key, prefilling, len(drafts))
+        # Kept here, not on the SchedulerOutput: that object is pickled to
+        # every worker each step.
+        self.stamps[id(output)] = stamps
+        while len(self.stamps) > 64:
+            self.stamps.pop(next(iter(self.stamps)))
+
+    def begin_feedback(self):
+        self.feedback_time = time.perf_counter()
+
+    def feedback(self, output, request, drafted, accepted, output_tokens, valid):
+        rid = request.request_id
+        entry = self.active.get(rid)
+        stamp = self.stamps.get(id(output), {}).get(rid)
+        if entry is None or stamp is None or stamp[0] != entry.generation or entry.failed:
+            return
+        _, sent, key, prefilling, actual_k = stamp
+        now = self.feedback_time if self.feedback_time is not None else time.perf_counter()
+        previous = entry.previous
+        entry.previous = (now, key, prefilling, actual_k)
+        seconds = now - sent
+        timing_valid = bool(
+            valid
+            and not prefilling
+            and previous is not None
+            and previous[1] == key
+            and not previous[2]
